LOCAL PROOF\n# Started: 2026-08-09 18:31:50 +03:00\n# Command: bun loop/items/AI4DEV-59/proof-local.ts\n# Worktree: C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Downloads\\ai4good\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-aa95110cbeab31aa7\n# Branch:   nirdrang/ai4dev-59-email-verification-and-the-gate-on-unverified-writing-d2l1\n# Result:   7 checks - 7 passed - 0 failed - 0 skipped - exit code 0. ONE RUN, no re-run.\n#\n# WHAT THIS TRANSCRIPT IS. The only evidence in this item about the real Supabase Auth under\n# [auth.email] enable_confirmations = true, the real confirmation email, and the real /auth/v1/user\n# serialisation the shipped extractor has to read. It was produced on ONE machine, by hand, once. A\n# reviewer cannot reproduce it; it is one machine's word, and it is written that way rather than\n# dressed up.\n#\n# WHAT WAS RUNNING. The local Supabase stack, STOPPED AND STARTED so that the auth container was\n# created from this branch's config.toml, then the migrations replayed from empty\n# (bun run db:reset, exit 0), and the edge functions served from THIS worktree by\n# bunx supabase functions serve, without --no-verify-jwt. loop/items/AI4DEV-59/stack-up.txt is that\n# record, and it carries the readings that prove the flip is live: the auth container answered\n# GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=true before the restart (confirmations OFF) and\n# GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=false after it (confirmations ON).","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Downloads\\ai4good\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-aa95110cbeab31aa7\\loop\\items\\AI4DEV-59\\proof-local.txt","text":"# AI4DEV-59 (email verification, unverified-write gate) - STEP 5, THE LIVE LOCAL PROOF\n# Started: 2026-08-09 18:31:50 +03:00\n# Command: bun loop/items/AI4DEV-59/proof-local.ts\n# Worktree: C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Downloads\\ai4good\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-aa95110cbeab31aa7\n# Branch:   nirdrang/ai4dev-59-email-verification-and-the-gate-on-unverified-writing-d2l1\n# Result:   7 checks - 7 passed - 0 failed - 0 skipped - exit code 0. ONE RUN, no re-run.\n#\n# WHAT THIS TRANSCRIPT IS. The only evidence in this item about the real Supabase Auth under\n# [auth.email] enable_confirmations = true, the real confirmation email, and the real /auth/v1/user\n# serialisation the shipped extractor has to read. It was produced on ONE machine, by hand, once. A\n# reviewer cannot reproduce it; it is one machine's word, and it is written that way rather than\n# dressed up.\n#\n# WHAT WAS RUNNING. The local Supabase stack, STOPPED AND STARTED so that the auth container was\n# created from this branch's config.toml, then the migrations replayed from empty\n# (bun run db:reset, exit 0), and the edge functions served from THIS worktree by\n# bunx supabase functions serve, without --no-verify-jwt. loop/items/AI4DEV-59/stack-up.txt is that\n# record, and it carries the readings that prove the flip is live: the auth container answered\n# GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=true before the restart (confirmations OFF) and\n# GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=false after it (confirmations ON).\n#\n# NO KEY MATERIAL APPEARS BELOW, and it is designed in rather than scrubbed afterwards. The script\n# reads every key from supabase status -o json at run time and prints none of them. Redaction covers\n# three surfaces after the second review gate: object bodies by key name, STRINGS (JWT-shaped runs\n# and credential-named name=value pairs), and the printed redirect location, whose fragment is cut\n# and whose every query-parameter VALUE is replaced.\n#\n# THE INSPECTION THAT RULING ASKS FOR, performed on this file before it was committed. Searched for:\n# eyJ, sb_secret, sb_publishable, access_token, refresh_token, token=, token_hash, provider_token,\n# apikey, JWT_SECRET, super-secret, S3_PROTOCOL, \"Bearer \", password, otp, nonce - and for any\n# base64url-shaped run of 40 characters or more. RESULT: zero hits for every pattern except one\n# occurrence of \"password\", which is the phrase \"email/password signup\" in check (a)'s own title.\n# Zero long base64url-shaped runs. No credential residue.\n#\n# WHAT NO GREEN HERE CLAIMS: that any deployed route enforces the Discovery gate - none exists, and\n# no check below exercises discoveryMessageAllowed; that hosted email delivery works - only the\n# local mail catcher was read; that any screen exists; anything about link expiry, single use or\n# resend - retired AT-001.11's semantics, deliberately unasserted; or anything about a provider\n# (Google, GitHub) user's verified state - no OAuth credential exists in this environment.\n#\n# THREE MEASUREMENTS WORTH READING TWICE:\n#   1. GoTrue's pre-confirmation sign-in refusal is HTTP 400 with error_code \"email_not_confirmed\" -\n#      exactly the discriminator check (c) pins. The expectation was pinned BEFORE the run and did\n#      not have to be corrected afterwards.\n#   2. The mail catcher behind port 54324 is MAILPIT v1.30.2, measured by probing both known API\n#      shapes. The Inbucket shape answered 404.\n#   3. The tampered-token probe, check (b2): GoTrue answered the never-issued token with a 303 to\n#      the site URL, and auth.users.email_confirmed_at stayed NULL. The column is the fact; the\n#      status is recorded but not asserted on.\n\n\nmail catcher shape, measured: mailpit\n        catcher at http://127.0.0.1:54324 · GET /api/v1/info -> HTTP 200 \"{\\\"Version\\\":\\\"v1.30.2\\\",\\\"LatestVersion\\\":\\\"v1.30.7\\\",\\\"Database\\\":\\\"/tmp/mailpit-1786289347825166043.db\\\",\\\"DatabaseSize\\\":94208,\\\"Messages\\\":0,\\\"Unread\\\":0,\\\"Tags\\\":{},\\\"RuntimeStats\\\":{\\\"Uptime\\\":161,\\\"Memory\\\":11540744,\\\"M\" · GET /api/v1/mailbox/probe -> HTTP 404 \"File not found\\n\"\n\nPASS  (a) an email/password signup under enable_confirmations = true returns NO session, and auth.users.email_confirmed_at is NULL\n        signup HTTP 200 {\"id\":\"2b5c6886-e9fe-4a22-90ff-3881d08227a3\",\"aud\":\"authenticated\",\"role\":\"authenticated\",\"email\":\"ng