ady running was created BEFORE this branch flipped\n17: # [auth.email] enable_confirmations to true, and its container proved it - the reading is the\n18: # first command below. A db reset alone would have left that container in place, and every\n19: # check in step 5 would have measured the OLD setting.\n20: \n21: ===== BEFORE: the running auth container's confirmation setting - GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=true means confirmations are OFF =====\n22: $ docker inspect supabase_auth_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | Select-String -Pattern \"AUTOCONFIRM|RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL\"\n23: \n24: GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=true\n25: GOTRUE_SMS_AUTOCONFIRM=true\n26: GOTRUE_RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL_SENT=360000\n27: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n28: \n29: ===== bun run db:stop =====\n30: $ bun run db:stop\n31: bun : $ bunx supabase stop\n32: At line:1 char:1\n33: + bun run db:stop\n34: + ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n35:     + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: ($ bunx supabase stop:String) [], RemoteException\n36:     + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n37:  \n38: {\"project_id_filter\":\"poancmeitlmxejofwzuu\",\"backup\":true,\"message\":\"Stopped supabase local development setup.\"}\n39: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n40: \n41: ===== bun run db:start - the stack comes back up, and its auth container is created from THIS branch's config.toml =====\n42: $ bun run db:start\n43: bun : $ bunx supabase start\n44: At line:1 char:1\n45: + bun run db:start\n46: + ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n47:     + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: ($ bunx supabase start:String) [], RemoteException\n48:     + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n49:  \n50: {\"DB_URL\":\"postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres\",\"API_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321\",\"REST_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/rest/v1\",\"GRAPHQL_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/graphql/v1\",\"FUNCTIONS_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1\",\"MCP_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/mcp\",\"STUDIO_URL\":\"ht