0c389c633b9867b93b1466a77c75d5bc9df66f56:loop/items/AI4DEV-60/artifacts/audit-luna.stderr.log:7917:loop/items/AI4DEV-59/artifacts/audit-luna.stderr.log:10239:C:\Users\nirdr\Downloads\ai4good\.claude\worktrees\agent-aa95110cbeab31aa7\loop\items\AI4DEV-59\artifacts\audit-flash.events.jsonl:2:{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786290388882,"sessionID":"ses_018cbdef8ffeIiDUqdR6dh2IlP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_FIjuOluyW2NhJc9NRS7f2224","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Downloads\\ai4good\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-aa95110cbeab31aa7\\loop\\items\\AI4DEV-59\\plan.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Downloads\\ai4good\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-aa95110cbeab31aa7\\loop\\items\\AI4DEV-59\\plan.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # AI4DEV-59 (email verification, unverified-write gate) — PLAN\n2: \n3: **Sitting 1 of the item: PLAN. Ruled by the `orchestrator` definition on fable (claude-fable-5,\n4: effort xhigh).**\n5: \n6: **Sitting 2 (DRAFT, same definition and model) ruled on gate 1's four findings and amended this\n7: plan. The rulings are section 7. The amended text below is what gets built; the pre-amendment\n8: text is commit `46b7485`.**\n9: \n10: **Sitting 3 (FIX AND GOAL, same definition and model) ruled on gate 2's twelve findings — nine\n11: from seat A, three from seat B, two convergent pairs. The rulings are section 8. That sitting\n12: amended step 2's mirror-binding sentence and step 5's done-list; the pre-amendment text is\n13: commit `ac33db1`.**\n14: \n15: **Chain, derived from the branch**\n16: (`nirdrang/ai4dev-59-email-verification-and-the-gate-on-unverified-writing-d2l1`):\n17: AI4DEV-59 (email verification, unverified-write gate) → AI4DEV-52 (verification, sessions and\n18: reset container) → AI4DEV-50 (auth dev-tree root) → AI4PM-19 (the authentication requirement).\n19: No `attr:` label on any of them; product work with an evidence gate above it.\n20: \n21: **Manifest:** `loop/decomp/req-001.md`, deliverable D2 leaf L1, revision `0579425`:\n22: *\"verification flow (all email-capable account types) + unverified-write gate on Discovery\n23: messages · verify: AT-001.09,10 · blocked-by: D1.L1\"*. The D1 container is Done on the board\n24: (its two leaves merged as pull requests #47 and #48), so the blocker is cleared.\n25: \n26: **Acceptance ids this leaf owns:** AT-001.09, AT-001.10.\n27: **Acceptance text (read-only for this item):** `.taskmaster/docs/acceptance/at-req-001.md`\n28: lines 20–21. Line 22 matters too: **AT-001.11 is retired** — *\"verification-link\n29: expiry/single-use/resend semantics are not stated in REQ-001\"* — so no assertion in this item\n30: may claim those semantics.\n31: \n32: **Ratified product text behind the gate:** the PRD makes email verification *\"the floor for any\n33: Discovery message\"* and says vetting is *\"never the Discovery wall\"* (decision-8,\n34: `.taskmaster/docs/prd-new.md` line 787; also lines 155 and 159, and\n35: `.taskmaster/docs/prd-mvp.md` line 157).\n36: \n37: **Verify command, pinned:** `bun run at:verify req-001 --tier loop --expect`. The fixture\n38: adapter is a stand-in capped at the loop tier (its own header, `_fixture.ts` lines 7–10;\n39: `adapterDerivedCapability()` in `tests/at/harness/capabilities.ts`), CI has no database, and the\n40: requirement's integration-tier done contract remains AI4PM-19's gate, not this leaf's.\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 1. What I verified in the tree before deciding anything\n45: \n46: | claim | verdict | evidence (pointer) |\n47: |---|---|---|\n48: | Both ids are declared red, pending on this leaf | true | `tests/at/expected/req-001.json` lines 15–16; stubs at `tests/at/suites/req-001/b-verification-and-sessions.test.ts` lines 13 and 15, each `notLanded(LEAF.D2_L1)` |\n49: | The config flip is reserved for this leaf | true | `supabase/config.toml` line 243 `enable_confirmations = false`; the b-file header (lines 4–7) says turning it on \"is the verification leaf's own change\" |\n50: | A local mail catcher is enabled | true | `supabase/config.toml` lines 105–108: `[local_smtp]` enabled, web interface on port 54324 |\n51: | The local stack limits auth emails to 2 per hour | true (as configured) | `supabase/config.toml` line 216, `[auth.rate_limit] email_sent = 2`; whether it binds with the local test mailer is measured in step 5, not assumed |\n52: | No Discovery product code exists anywhere | true | grep `discovery` over `supabase/`, `src/`, `tests/` — only docs, a harness rubric for another requirement, and this suite's own stub title; the future route is mapped to a `discovery-message` edge function in `.taskmaster/docs/migration-nextjs-to-tanstack-VERIFIED.md` lines 103–105 |\n53: | The decision-module pattern is established: shipped judgements, fixture storage | true | `supabase/functions/_shared/accounts.ts` header; `_fixture.ts` header and its imports (lines 45–62) |\n54: | The suite already models \"the hook a later leaf must call\" | true | `hasPlatformAcknowledgment`'s contract comment, `_contract.ts` lines 244–260 — enforcement it cannot build is named as the hook the later leaf calls |\n55: | The caller-fact-through-shipped-extractor pattern is ratified | true | `_fixture.ts` lines 208–225 (gate-2 ruling R3 of the GitHub leaf): the fixture renders the canonical GoTrue user shape and derives the fact through the shipped extractor |\n56: | `_pending.ts` header counts will go stale | true | `tests/at/suites/req-001/_pending.ts` lines 3 and 9 say 30 pending / seven written; after this item it is 28 / nine |\n57: | CI runs typecheck, harness self-tests, at:check and at:verify (loop, --expect) per suite, plus the ownership and reference guards | true | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` |\n58: | GoTrue with confirmations on issues no session at signup and refuses sign-in until the address is confirmed | **unverified-runtime-claim** | expected GoTrue behaviour; measured, with exact refusal text captured, in step 5 — nothing in this plan silently depends on it before then |\n59: \n60: ## 2. Decisions\n61: \n62: ### D-A — \"Verified\" is Supabase Auth's own fact. No migration, no new column.\n63: The observable behind AT-001.09 is `email_confirmed_at` on the auth user — GoTrue's field, set\n64: by GoTrue when the emailed link is used. Nothing this leaf ships writes it, `public.accounts`\n65: gains no column, and this item ships **no migration**. Consequence: there is no schema, RLS or\n66: privilege surface to prove here; the live proof reads `auth.users.email_confirmed_at` as\n67: operator evidence only.\n68: \n69: ### D-B — The config flip, and one pre-authorized relief valve\n70: `[auth.email] enable_confirmations` flips to `true` in `supabase/config.toml` — the change the\n71: b-file header explicitly reserves for this leaf. The comment beside it is updated to say what it\n72: changes and which leaf owns it. **Pre-authorized amendment:** if step 5's registrations starve\n73: on the 2-per-hour `[auth.rate_limit] email_sent` limit (429 or absent mail), the executor raises\n74: that value (e.g. to 100) in the same file, restarts the stack, and records the raise in the\n75: transcript. This is local-stack configuration; no hosted deployment exists.\n76: \n77: ### D-C — The gate is a shipped decision module: `supabase/functions/_shared/verification.ts`\n78: A new module under the same two constraints as `accounts.ts` (relative imports only, no Deno\n79: global, no I/O; its type coverage is its import from the acceptance program). Two exports:\n80: \n81: - `emailVerifiedFromUser(user: unknown): boolean` — judges the GoTrue `/auth/v1/user` response\n82:   shape: a non-empty string `email_confirmed_at` means verified; **anything else — missing\n83:   field, null, non-string, malformed object — means unverified.** Fail closed.\n84: - `discoveryMessageAllowed(caller: { emailVerified: boolean }): Decision<'verified'>` —\n85:   `Decision` imported from `./accounts.ts`. The ONLY allow is `caller?.emailVerified === true`;\n86:   a missing or malformed caller argument refuses (the same fail-closed posture, for the same\n87:   measured reason: edge entry points have no type-checker). The refusal reason names email\n88:   verification as what is missing AND as the remedy, in words AT-001.10's assertion can match.\n89: \n90: The gate is **type-blind**: decision-8 makes verification the floor for ANY Discovery message.\n91: AT-001.10's unverified-NGO subject is an instance of that rule, not its scope, and a gate that\n92: read the account type would be shipping a distinction no ratified text draws.\n93: \n94: Why a new module rather than growing `accounts.ts`: that file's header scopes it to the account\n95: deliverable's decisions; `github.ts` already set the several-small-modules precedent; and this\n96: rule's future caller is the Discovery send route, not signup.\n97: \n98: ### D-D — No Discovery surface ships. The gate is the hook the route must call.\n99: The Discovery message route belongs to REQ-002/004 (the migration doc maps it to a future\n100: `discovery-message` edge function). Building an edge function or a table for it here would be\n101: another requirement's surface invented early. What this leaf ships is the **decision** that\n102: route must consult — exactly the pattern the suite already ratifies for\n103: `hasPlatformAcknowledgment` (\"this is the hook the leaf that lands project creation must call\").\n104: The module header and section 4 both state it plainly: **the gate has no deployed caller yet**,\n105: and no green from this item may be read as \"Discovery messaging is gated in production.\"\n106: \n107: At the loop tier the SUT gains a `sendDiscoveryMessage` operation and the fixture is the\n108: stand-in surface: it renders the caller's GoTrue user shape from stored Auth state, derives the\n109: verified fact through the SHIPPED `emailVerifiedFromUser`, consults the SHIPPED\n110: `discoveryMessageAllowed`, refuses with the gate's own reason and **writes nothing**, or on\n111: allow records the message in fixture storage. Every judgement is the shipped module's; the\n112: storage is a Map like all the rest.\n113: \n114: ### D-E — Fixture and contract: mirror Auth's verification state, judge nothing\n115: `_fixture.ts`: `AuthUser` gains `emailConfirmedAt: string | null` and\n116: `verificationLink: string | null`. An email/password registration starts unconfirmed and mints\n117: a link value (the fixture's stand-in for the emailed link the mail catcher would hold). A\n118: provider registration (Google/GitHub) starts confirmed — the expected GoTrue behaviour when the\n119: provider vouches for the address. **This mirror is UNBOUND by this item** (gate-1 ruling [1],\n120: section 7): no OAuth app or credential exists in this environment, so no live provider session\n121: is obtainable — the same recorded gap that leaves the OAuth handshake itself unproved at every\n122: tier, stated in the fixture header since the predecessor. No test this item reads a provider\n123: user's verified state; both new bodies register by email/password. If the prediction is wrong —\n124: a real provider user arriving unconfirmed — the shipped gate fails closed: it refuses, never\n125: allows. The fixture header's mirror section states all of this; the mirror is bound by the\n126: first item that ships a real provider-path consumer.\n127: \n128: `_contract.ts`: `AccountsSut` gains five members —\n129: - `emailVerified(accountId): Promise<boolean>` — read-back, derived through the shipped\n130:   `emailVerifiedFromUser` over the rendered GoTrue user shape (the R3 pattern: the extractor\n131:   sits on the tested path, exactly as the future route's caller resolution would).\n132: - `emailedVerificationLink(email): Promise<string | null>` — the emailed verification link for\n133:   the address, or null when none was emailed.\n134: - `useVerificationLink(link): Promise<{ ok: boolean }>` — using an emailed link confirms the\n135:   address; a never-issued link returns `ok: false` and flips nothing. **No expiry, no\n136:   single-use, no resend is modelled or asserted — those are retired AT-001.11's semantics,\n137:   deliberately unstated in REQ-001.** The never-issued negative is not AT-001.11 ground: a\n138:   link-shaped string that verifies an account it never belonged to would make \"using the link\n139:   flips it\" meaningless, so the negative guards this test's own oracle.\n140: - `sendDiscoveryMessage(session, body: string): Promise<{ ok: true } | { ok: false; reason:\n141:   string }>` — per D-D. A caller with no completed account gets the fixture's bookkeeping\n142:   refusal, same shape as `createOrganization`'s.\n143: - `discoveryMessagesBy(accountId): Promise<string[]>` — read-back, because a block whose write\n144:   happened anyway is not a block.\n145: \n146: `registerWithEmailPassword` keeps returning a `Session`. The fixture's `Session` has always\n147: been an identity handle, not an access token — session ISSUANCE (and with it \"an unconfirmed\n148: user holds no session\") is D2.L2's subject. The honest gap this leaves is stated in section 4\n149: and in the test comments, not hidden: at the loop tier a completed-but-unverified account is\n150: constructible; on the live stack the public path cannot reach it (step 5 measures that).\n151: \n152: ### D-F — AT-001.09's body: parameterized over both types, surface `ui`\n153: For EACH of `ngo` and `volunteer` (the two email-capable public types —\n154: `PUBLIC_SIGNUP_ACCOUNT_TYPES`; the platform admin is provisioned, not signed up, and is outside\n155: this criterion's \"can register by email\"):\n156: 1. register with email/password → `emailVerified` is **false** — the fresh signup is\n157:    email-unverified.\n158: 2. complete signup (NGO with an organisation name; volunteer after `linkGithubIdentity`, the\n159:    precondition AT-001.04 owns) → the account row carries its type — which makes \"either\n160:    account type\" a fact of the run, not a label.\n161: 3. still `emailVerified` false — completion does not verify.\n162: 4. negative: `useVerificationLink('never-issued-link')` → `ok: false`, and `emailVerified`\n163:    still false.\n164: 5. `emailedVerificationLink(email)` → non-null; `useVerificationLink(link)` → `ok: true`;\n165:    `emailVerified` → **true** — using the emailed link is what flips it.\n166: 6. the account row still carries the same type — verification re-types nothing.\n167: \n168: Surface mark `ui`: the verification screen is one of the four auth screens the manifest's\n169: wiring leaf names (*\"signup, sign-in, verification, reset\"*), so D2.LW must find this id to\n170: re-run `--wired`.\n171: \n172: Ordering note, stated so the review can attack it rather than discover it: the test completes\n173: signup BEFORE verifying, so that the typed account is observably unverified — the criterion's\n174: \"the account … is email-unverified until the link is used\" read with \"account\" meaning the\n175: typed account. On the live stack with confirmations on the public order is verify-then-complete\n176: (no session exists before confirmation); step 5 drives THAT order against the real stack. The\n177: two orders together cover both readings; neither contradicts any criterion.\n178: \n179: ### D-G — AT-001.10's body: the discriminating pair, surface `backend`\n180: 1. register an NGO by email/password and complete signup **without verifying** (reachable at\n181:    the loop tier per D-E; the body's comment states plainly that the live public path cannot\n182:    reach this state and why the gate exists anyway — decision-8 makes the floor the write\n183:    path's own rule, not a property borrowed from the session layer, and non-public paths and\n184:    configuration history can produce exactly this state).\n185: 2. `sendDiscoveryMessage` → refused; the reason matches `/verif/i` and `/email/i` —\n186:    verification named as the remedy; `discoveryMessagesBy` is empty — the blocked attempt\n187:    wrote nothing.\n188: 3. the discriminating control: use the emailed verification link → `emailVerified` true → the\n189:    SAME send now succeeds and `discoveryMessagesBy` records it. The remedy is proved by being\n190:    the exact change that unblocks, and a refuse-everybody gate fails this half.\n191: \n192: Surface mark `backend`: the Discovery composer is REQ-002/004's surface; it is not one of the\n193: four auth screens, and the wiring leaf has nothing of it to re-run.\n194: \n195: ### D-H — Suite bookkeeping, all in the same change\n196: - `tests/at/expected/req-001.json`: AT-001.09 and AT-001.10 move from `red` to `green` — 9\n197:   green / 28 declared red.\n198: - `_pending.ts`: `D2_L1` is removed from `LEAF` (the orphan rule — its last two users become\n199:   real bodies), and the header's counts and \"seven are written\" sentence are corrected —\n200:   after this item they are false statements of fact, the audit's first box.\n201: - The b-file header is rewritten: its `enable_confirmations` sentence becomes false the moment\n202:   this leaf lands. `LEAF`/`notLanded` imports stay — four D2.L2 stubs still use them.\n203: - `loop/items/AI4DEV-59/pending-ledger.txt`: 28 lines, one per remaining pending id, each\n204:   naming a deliverable-and-leaf that appears in `loop/decomp/req-001.md`; this leaf's ids\n205:   absent.\n206: \n207: ### D-I — One review slice\n208: Estimated diff outside `loop/items/`: ~70 lines shared module, ~10 config, ~60 contract, ~90\n209: fixture, ~140 suite bodies and headers, ~50 shape selftest (gate-1 ruling [4]), ~15 declaration\n210: and pending bookkeeping — roughly 450.\n211: Far under the 1200-line trigger the previous two leaves used. **One slice**; both pinned\n212: draft-code readers read the whole diff.\n213: \n214: ## 3. Steps, each with its own done-criterion\n215: \n216: Item evidence lives in `loop/items/AI4DEV-59/`. Every path repository-relative. The executor\n217: commits one commit per step (the parking rule).\n218: \n219: **Step 0 — baseline.** `bun run typecheck`, `bun run at:selftest`, `bun run at:check req-001`,\n220: `bun run at:check req-016`, `bun run at:verify req-001 --tier loop --expect`,\n221: `bun run at:verify req-016 --tier loop --expect`.\n222: → done: all exit 0, transcript in `loop/items/AI4DEV-59/baseline.txt` (req-001 showing 7 green /\n223: 30 declared red). A red baseline is reported, not worked around.\n224: \n225: **Step 1 — the shipped gate.** `supabase/functions/_shared/verification.ts` per D-C, header\n226: naming the hook contract (D-D) and the fail-closed posture.\n227: → done: `bun run typecheck` exits 0 with the module imported by the acceptance program (via the\n228: fixture); the refusal reason names email verification as the remedy; and a direct shape test —\n229: `tests/at/harness/shipped-verification.selftest.ts` (gate-1 ruling [4], section 7) — proves the\n230: fail-closed promise: `emailVerifiedFromUser` returns false for a missing field, `null`, an\n231: empty string, a number, an object value, and a non-object user, and true only for a non-empty\n232: string; `discoveryMessageAllowed` refuses a missing and a malformed caller in the same file.\n233: The vitest include `harness/**/*.selftest.ts` and the `at:selftest` filter pick it up with zero\n234: script or CI change — verified against `tests/at/vitest.config.ts` line 16 and the\n235: `package.json` script. Its header states why a shipped module's shape test rides the selftest\n236: lane: the promise cannot arise through the fixture, and this lane is what CI already runs.\n237: \n238: **Step 2 — contract and fixture.** The D-E extensions, judgements delegated per D-C/D-D.\n239: → done (rewritten by gate-1 ruling [3], section 7 — the earlier criterion was unsatisfiable as\n240: written): `bun run typecheck` exits 0; both PRODUCT judgements — the verified-fact extraction\n241: and the Discovery gate — come only from the shipped `verification.ts`, with no second copy of\n242: either rule in the fixture; and every VENDOR MIRROR this leaf adds is named in the fixture\n243: header's mirror section with what binds it: link issuance at email signup is bound by step 5\n244: (a)–(b); a never-issued link returning `ok: false` is bound by step 5 (b2) — the tampered-link\n245: negative added by gate-2 rulings [A2]/[B1], section 8, because the earlier \"(a)–(d)\" wording\n246: claimed a binding no check measured; a used link setting `emailConfirmedAt` is bound by step 5\n247: (b) and (d); a provider registration starting confirmed is declared UNBOUND, per the D-E\n248: amendment; and the provisioned platform admin starting CONFIRMED mirrors the recorded\n249: provisioning recipe (gate-2 ruling [A8], section 8), read by nothing and live-bound by the\n250: first item that reads an admin's verified state.\n251: \n252: **Step 3 — the two real test bodies, and the bookkeeping.** D-F, D-G, D-H.\n253: → done: `bun run at:verify req-001 --tier loop --expect` exits 0 with exactly 9 passed and 28\n254: declared red; `bun run at:check req-001` clean; no comment in any touched file still states\n255: that .09/.10 are pending, that the config flip is reserved, or a stale count.\n256: \n257: **Step 4 — the config flip, and the stack with it.** D-B in `supabase/config.toml`; restart the\n258: local stack so auth picks it up.\n259: → done: `bun run db:reset` (or stop/start) completes; `bunx supabase status` shows the stack up;\n260: transcript in `loop/items/AI4DEV-59/stack-up.txt`. Two failed attempts → stop and report.\n261: \n262: **Step 5 — the live proof.** `loop/items/AI4DEV-59/proof-local.ts` against the live stack,\n263: transcript in `proof-local.txt`. Evidence-gathering, run once, never a guarding test. Secrets\n264: redacted exactly as the predecessor transcripts redact them.\n265: → done, all of:\n266:   (a) an email/password signup under the flipped config returns **no session**, and the\n267:   operator read on the database (port 54322) shows `auth.users.email_confirmed_at IS NULL` —\n268:   the unverified-runtime-claims from section 1 measured, with exact wire responses captured;\n269:   (b) the mail catcher on port 54324 holds the confirmation email for that address, and the\n270:   verification link is extracted from it — the catcher's API shape MEASURED first, not assumed;\n271:   (b2) a tampered variant of that link — its token altered, so a token GoTrue never issued —\n272:   is followed BEFORE the real one, and `auth.users.email_confirmed_at` stays NULL: the\n273:   never-issued-link mirror measured rather than inferred (gate-2 rulings [A2]/[B1], section 8);\n274:   no expiry, single-use or resend semantics are touched — the token followed was never issued.\n275:   If only the operator-minted fallback link exists, (b2) runs against a tampered variant of THAT\n276:   link with a note naming the source — a mutated operator-minted token is equally never-issued —\n277:   and it skips only when no link exists at all (sitting-3 ruling on the executor's report);\n278:   (c) sign-in BEFORE confirmation is refused with a CONFIRMATION-SPECIFIC refusal — a 4xx whose\n279:   body names the unconfirmed state (expected GoTrue error code `email_not_confirmed`), captured\n280:   verbatim; a 429 or a 5xx is NOT this refusal and fails the check (gate-2 ruling [A3], section\n281:   8). The discriminator is read from the in-memory body, because the transcript redactor's\n282:   name-pattern also blanks `error_code`, and the note surfaces it through a safe extraction;\n283:   (d) using the link (HTTP GET) flips `email_confirmed_at` to non-null; sign-in now succeeds;\n284:   and the raw `/auth/v1/user` response of the signed-in user, fed to the SHIPPED\n285:   `emailVerifiedFromUser`, returns true — the extractor bound to GoTrue's real serialisation\n286:   (its false half is exercised at the loop tier; an unconfirmed user has no session to read\n287:   `/auth/v1/user` with, and the transcript says so rather than dressing it up);\n288:   (e) both email-capable types flow END TO END under the flipped config (gate-1 ruling [2],\n289:   section 7 — the flip changes the auth context beneath BOTH completion paths, so the\n290:   predecessor's completion evidence predates it and is re-proved, not cited): a second address\n291:   repeats (a)–(d); the NGO address completes signup through the deployed `complete-signup`\n292:   edge function AFTER confirmation; the volunteer address, after confirmation and sign-in,\n293:   gains a GitHub identity by the predecessor's mechanism — the operator-authority insert into\n294:   `auth.identities` (`fabricateGithubIdentity` in the predecessor's proof script, flip-\n295:   independent because it is a database write, not an auth flow) — then completes as a\n296:   volunteer through the same deployed function, and the account row and imported profile are\n297:   read back. The volunteer's \"repeats (a)–(d)\" claim has teeth (gate-2 rulings [A3]/[A4],\n298:   section 8): its link MUST come from the catcher (`linkSource === 'emailed'`) and its\n299:   pre-confirmation sign-in refusal MUST be the same confirmation-specific one as (c);\n300:   (f) if the mailer rate limit starves (b), the D-B relief valve fires and the transcript\n301:   records it.\n302: \n303: **Step 6 — the whole verify surface, green together.** The step-0 list re-run.\n304: → done: all exit 0 in `loop/items/AI4DEV-59/verify-final.txt`; req-016 unchanged from baseline.\n305: \n306: ## 4. Expected verification state, per acceptance-test id\n307: \n308: At `bun run at:verify req-001 --tier loop --expect` when this item is done: **AT-001.01–.07,\n309: .09, .10 green (9), the other 28 P0 ids red as `{\"kind\":\"pending\",\"phase\":\"sut-missing\"}`**,\n310: exit 0.\n311: \n312: | id | proved at loop tier (CI) | proved on the live stack (step 5, one machine) | **not proved by this item** |\n313: |---|---|---|---|\n314: | AT-001.09 | the flow shape against the fixture's Auth mirror: both public types start email-unverified, a never-issued link flips nothing, the emailed link flips the account to verified, the type survives; the shipped `emailVerifiedFromUser` judges the rendered user shape on every read | the real substance: GoTrue issues no session at signup, the confirmation email exists and its link flips `email_confirmed_at`, sign-in is refused before and succeeds after, the shipped extractor answers true against GoTrue's real serialisation | email delivery anywhere but the local mail catcher; any screen (D2.LW's, and Lovable's territory); link expiry / single-use / resend semantics — retired AT-001.11, deliberately unasserted; GoTrue's serialisation of provider-vouched confirmation — the fixture's provider-confirmed start is an unbound vendor mirror (D-E amendment) |\n315: | AT-001.10 | the SHIPPED gate refuses an unverified account's Discovery send with verification named as the remedy and writes nothing, and the SAME send succeeds once verified — the discriminating pair | the auth-layer fact: an unconfirmed email/password user cannot authenticate at all, refusal text captured — on the live stack the block sits upstream of the gate | **enforcement at a deployed Discovery route — none exists.** The route is REQ-002/004's; the gate is the hook it must call, stated in the module header. No green here may be read as \"Discovery messaging is gated in production\" |\n316: | AT-001.01–.07 | unchanged claims, bodies untouched | (e) re-proves BOTH public email paths end to end under the flipped config — NGO completion, and volunteer GitHub-link-then-completion; everything else is the predecessors' record | unchanged from the predecessors' tables |\n317: \n318: **What the green does and does not claim** (repeated in the merge ruling): claims — the two\n319: tests exist, execute, open worlds and assert; the shipped decision module `verification.ts` —\n320: byte for byte the code a future route imports — behaves as the two criteria require, and fails\n321: closed; the config flip is real and the live verification round trip works on one machine.\n322: Does not claim — that any deployed route enforces the gate (none exists to), that hosted email\n323: delivery works, that any screen exists, or anything about session expiry, revocation, refresh\n324: or password reset (D2.L2's ids, declared red).\n325: \n326: ## 5. Seen, deliberately not touched\n327: \n328: - **The a-file's seven green tests.** No criterion makes completion require verification, and\n329:   the fixture does not model session issuance, so no existing body changes. The live-stack\n330:   consequence of the flip (no session until confirmed) is proved as (e), not simulated at loop.\n331: - **Session semantics** — expiry, revocation, refresh, reset: D2.L2's four ids, still\n332:   `notLanded(LEAF.D2_L2)`.\n333: - **The wiring leaf's screens**, including the verify CTA the PRD describes — D2.LW, and\n334:   `src/` is the other ownership territory besides.\n335: - **Retired AT-001.11 semantics** — nothing modelled, nothing asserted (D-E).\n336: - **The two filed items under the auth root** — the default-privilege residue on the four auth\n337:   tables, and the volunteer GitHub-unlink enforcement — other items' work.\n338: - The acceptance file and the manifest — read-only here; changes go through `/doc-sync`.\n339: - `AGENTS.md` staleness — pre-existing, filed two items ago, still not this item's.\n340: \n341: ## 6. Risks that could force a mid-flight change\n342: \n343: 1. **GoTrue's confirmations-on behaviour differs from the expectation** — a session at signup,\n344:    sign-in not refused, or a different `/auth/v1/user` serialisation. Step 5 measures all\n345:    three; if any differs, the plan is amended in the open, never silently thinned. The gate\n346:    module is unaffected either way (it judges a shape, and its fail-closed answer to a missing\n347:    field is the point).\n348: 2. **The mail catcher's API shape varies across CLI versions.** The executor measures the\n349:    endpoint before asserting (b). Fallback if the catcher cannot yield the link: GoTrue's admin\n350:    generate-link endpoint mints an equivalent verification link with operator authority — and\n351:    the transcript then says the EMAILED link was not what was followed, narrowing claim (b)\n352:    honestly instead of dressing it up.\n353: 3. **The email rate limit starves the proof.** The D-B relief valve is pre-authorized; the\n354:    transcript records the raise.\n355: 4. **The flip breaks an existing live flow.** Step 5(e) exists precisely to catch the plausible\n356:    ones (email/password signup → completion, for both public types). Anything else it surfaces is reported with the\n357:    evidence, classified, and ruled — not patched silently.\n358: 5. **The two bodies cannot be written without inventing Discovery semantics.** The send\n359:    operation carries an opaque string and nothing else; if anything richer turns out to be\n360:    needed, stop and report — richer semantics belong to REQ-002/004.\n361: \n362: ## 7. Gate 1 rulings (sitting 2, DRAFT — fable, claude-fable-5, effort xhigh)\n363: \n364: The gate had one reader. Its raw output is\n365: `loop/items/AI4DEV-59/artifacts/gate1-sol-output.md`; the distillate beside it matches the raw\n366: count (4 = 4). Every claim below is quoted verbatim from the raw output.\n367: \n368: **[1] severity high — ACCEPT, FIXED DIFFERENTLY.**\n369: Claim: \"The plan treats Google/GitHub users as email-confirmed without a ratified product\n370: ruling and incorrectly says step 5 verifies their GoTrue serialization, although that step\n371: exercises only email/password users.\"\n372: The second half is right and the plan text was false as written: step 5 has no OAuth flow, so\n373: it binds nothing about provider users. That sentence is removed (D-E amendment). The proposed\n374: remedy — raw `/auth/v1/user` responses from real Google and GitHub sessions — is not\n375: obtainable: no OAuth app or credential exists in this environment, the same recorded gap that\n376: leaves the OAuth handshake itself unproved at every tier (the fixture header has carried that\n377: statement since the predecessor item; this narrowing rides on that recorded gap rather than\n378: filing a duplicate). The first half needs no new product ruling: decision D-A already defines\n379: \"verified\" as GoTrue's own fact, so the fixture's provider-confirmed start is a prediction of\n380: the vendor, not a product choice this plan makes. No test this item reads a provider user's\n381: verified state, and if the prediction is wrong the shipped gate fails closed — a real\n382: unconfirmed provider user is refused, never allowed. The fix as built: the mirror is declared\n383: UNBOUND in D-E, in the fixture header's mirror section, and in section 4's not-proved column.\n384: \n385: **[2] severity medium — ACCEPT.**\n386: Claim: \"Step 5 claims both email-capable account types flow, but only the NGO address\n387: completes signup; the second address repeats type-blind Auth operations and never becomes a\n388: volunteer account.\"\n389: Correct, and the reviewer's reasoning is adopted whole: the config flip changes the auth\n390: context beneath both completion paths, so the predecessor's volunteer evidence — produced\n391: with confirmations off — predates the flip and no longer covers it. Step 5(e) is rewritten:\n392: the second address confirms, signs in, gains a GitHub identity through the predecessor's\n393: operator-authority insert into `auth.identities`, completes as a volunteer through the\n394: deployed function, and the account row and imported profile are read back.\n395: \n396: **[3] severity medium — ACCEPT, FIXED DIFFERENTLY.**\n397: Claim: \"Step 2's done-criterion that every fixture rule comes from a shipped module is\n398: impossible because the planned fixture itself decides link issuance, link validity,\n399: confirmation mutation, and provider auto-confirmation.\"\n400: Correct that the criterion was unsatisfiable read literally — the fixture necessarily mirrors\n401: vendor behaviour, and its own header already keeps a named mirror category. The remedy is not\n402: to drop the discipline but to state the real one: step 2's criterion is rewritten so that the\n403: two PRODUCT judgements come only from the shipped `verification.ts`, and every vendor mirror\n404: this leaf adds is named in the header's mirror section with what binds it. Three of the four\n405: named behaviours are bound by step 5 (a)–(d) on the live stack; provider auto-confirmation is\n406: declared UNBOUND per ruling [1] — bound \"to live evidence\" is met where live evidence is\n407: obtainable and honestly declined where it is not.\n408: \n409: **[4] severity medium — ACCEPT.**\n410: Claim: \"The promised fail-closed handling of missing, non-string, and malformed\n411: `email_confirmed_at` values has no planned oracle because the tests exercise only `null` and a\n412: valid timestamp string.\"\n413: Correct — a promise without an oracle is exactly what the audit would flag as an untrue stated\n414: fact, and weakening the promise would invert the gate's point. The fix: a direct shape test,\n415: `tests/at/harness/shipped-verification.selftest.ts`, added to step 1's done-criterion,\n416: covering the malformed shapes for `emailVerifiedFromUser` and the malformed-caller refusals\n417: for `discoveryMessageAllowed`. Placement verified before ruling: the vitest include\n418: `harness/**/*.selftest.ts` (`tests/at/vitest.config.ts` line 16) and the `at:selftest` filter\n419: pick the file up with zero script or CI change.\n420: \n421: No ruling removes work, so no removal-verification conditions exist. Nothing contradicts\n422: ratified text and nothing grows scope; there is no founder question.\n423: \n424: ## 8. Gate 2 rulings (sitting 3, FIX AND GOAL — fable, claude-fable-5, effort xhigh)\n425: \n426: The gate was a panel of two, each blind to the other. Seat A: nine findings, raw output\n427: `loop/items/AI4DEV-59/artifacts/gate2-terra-output.md`, distillate beside it (9 = 9). Seat B:\n428: three findings, raw output `loop/items/AI4DEV-59/artifacts/gate2-flash-output.md`, distillate\n429: beside it (3 = 3). Seat B also names seven verified-sound areas in its raw output — the\n430: fail-closed oracle coverage, the fixture discipline, AT-001.10's discriminating pair,\n431: AT-001.09's ordering, the bookkeeping counts, the refactor's neutrality, and the selftest-lane\n432: placement — recorded here as evidence, not as findings. Every claim below is quoted verbatim\n433: from the seat's raw output. TWO CONVERGENT PAIRS — [A2]+[B1] and [A6]+[B2] — two blind seats\n434: independently finding the same defect, the strongest signal a panel gives; each pair is one\n435: defect with one fix. **Twelve findings, twelve accepted (three of them fixed differently), zero\n436: rejected — ten distinct defects.**\n437: \n438: **[A2] + [B1] — CONVERGENT. ACCEPT.**\n439: Seat A (medium): \"The fixture calls the never-issued-link mirror live-bound even though the\n440: proof never follows or observes an unissued link.\"\n441: Seat B (low): \"Mirror 2 — 'a link that was never issued confirms nothing' — is labeled\n442: **BOUND** by the live proof, but none of proof checks (a)–(d) ever attempts a never-issued\n443: link, so nothing in the named evidence measures the negative.\"\n444: Both are right: mirror 2's BOUND label cited evidence that measured only the positive half, and\n445: the step-2 criterion's \"(a)–(d)\" wording carried the same overstatement into this plan. Seat\n446: A's proposed instrument is adopted — a mutated issued link is a token GoTrue never issued, and\n447: following it asserts nothing about expiry, single use or resend (retired AT-001.11 stays\n448: untouched). The fix: new proof check (b2) follows a tampered variant of the emailed link BEFORE\n449: the real one and requires `email_confirmed_at` still NULL; mirror 2's header entry cites (b2);\n450: step 2's criterion is amended (see section 3). The record was false as written and is corrected\n451: in the open, not thinned. Interpretation ruled after the build, upheld: (b2) skips only when NO\n452: link exists at all; when only the operator-minted fallback yields one, it runs against a\n453: tampered variant of that link with a note naming the source, because a mutated operator-minted\n454: token is equally a token GoTrue never issued. On the real run the link was emailed, so the\n455: question was moot.\n456: \n457: **[A1] — ACCEPT.** Seat A (medium): \"The malformed-caller selftest checks only `ok` and never\n458: verifies that those refusals name email verification as the remedy.\"\n459: Verified: `shipped-verification.selftest.ts` lines 96–114 assert only `.ok`. Today the module\n460: has ONE refusal literal covering every non-allow path, so the promise holds — but its oracle\n461: does not reach the malformed-caller paths, and a later split of the refusal paths would keep\n462: this selftest green while breaking the module header's all-refusals promise. Fix: assert\n463: `/verif/i` and `/email/i` on the reason of every malformed-caller refusal in that test.\n464: \n465: **[A3] — ACCEPT.** Seat A (high): \"Check (c) treats any HTTP status of 400 or greater as the\n466: expected pre-confirmation refusal and does not assert a confirmation-specific response.\"\n467: Verified: `ngoTrip.signInBefore.status >= 400` — a 429 or a 500 would record as PASS while\n468: confirmation enforced nothing. Fix: (c) passes only on a 4xx (never 5xx, never 429) whose body\n469: names the unconfirmed state — expected GoTrue error code `email_not_confirmed`, matched against\n470: the IN-MEMORY body because the transcript redactor's `code$` pattern blanks `error_code`; the\n471: note surfaces the discriminator through a safe extraction (an enum value, not a credential).\n472: If the live text differs, the check FAILS, the verbatim capture shows the real discriminator,\n473: and the executor pins that exact discriminator and re-runs — measurement, not assumption. The\n474: same tightening applies to the volunteer's pre-confirmation sign-in inside (e).\n475: \n476: **[A4] — ACCEPT.** Seat A (high): \"Check (e) never requires the volunteer round trip to use an\n477: emailed verification link, despite claiming it repeats check (b).\"\n478: Verified: (e)'s conjunction never reads `volunteerTrip.linkSource`, so the admin-generated\n479: fallback could pass (e) while the claim \"repeats (a)–(d)\" silently narrowed. The NGO half\n480: cannot do this — (b) fails with a NARROWED note on the fallback — so the volunteer half gets\n481: the same teeth: (e) requires `volunteerTrip.linkSource === 'emailed'`.\n482: \n483: **[A5] — ACCEPT, FIXED DIFFERENTLY, with a verification condition.** Seat A (medium): \"The\n484: stale-worktree probe accepts any non-404 response as the current `complete-signup` function.\"\n485: The fact is right — the probe fails only on 404 or unreachable, and a stale mount answers 401.\n486: The proposed remedy — a verifiable revision/source marker in the mounted artifact — buys\n487: revision-binding that (e)'s evidence does not depend on: this branch changes nothing under\n488: `supabase/functions/` except the NEW `_shared/verification.ts`, which `complete-signup` does\n489: not import, so any live `complete-signup` is byte-for-byte the code this branch carries.\n490: **VERIFY FIRST, before relying on that:** the executor confirms with\n491: `git diff main...HEAD --stat -- supabase/functions/` and by reading `complete-signup`'s\n492: imports. If the condition fails, this ruling's fixed-differently route is VOID — stop and\n493: report, and the full revision-binding remedy applies. If it holds: the probe's comment states\n494: the revision-independence argument, and `stack-up.txt` records the `functions serve` launch\n495: (command and cwd) as the operator-side binding of the mount to this worktree.\n496: \n497: **[A6] + [B2] — CONVERGENT. ACCEPT, at seat A's severity (high).**\n498: Seat A: \"The redirect redactor strips only URL fragments and logs credential-bearing query\n499: parameters unchanged.\"\n500: Seat B: \"The header promises 'NO KEY IS WRITTEN INTO THIS FILE AND NONE IS PRINTED BY IT', but\n501: the followed redirect's `location` is printed after only fragment-stripping\n502: (`withoutFragment`), and `redact()` returns non-object values — including non-JSON response\n503: bodies — verbatim.\"\n504: Both right, and seat B widens the surface to raw string bodies. One fix, three parts: (i) every\n505: query-parameter VALUE in a printed location header is redacted, names kept — a token-hash or\n506: `?code=` redirect can no longer land in a transcript; (ii) `redact()` scrubs strings too —\n507: JWT-shaped substrings (`eyJ…`) and `name=value` pairs whose name matches the SENSITIVE pattern\n508: are replaced; (iii) the transcript is INSPECTED for credential residue before it is committed —\n509: the run this sitting performs is that inspection.\n510: \n511: **[A7] — ACCEPT.** Seat A (medium): \"The updated fixture header falsely says `verification.ts`\n512: is imported by edge functions and that every accept/refusal below comes from shipped modules.\"\n513: Verified: no deployed function imports `verification.ts` — that is decision D-D's own point —\n514: and `sendDiscoveryMessage`'s no-completed-account refusal is fixture bookkeeping, not a shipped\n515: judgement. This diff rewrote that header paragraph, so the falsehood is this item's to fix.\n516: Fix: the PROVED paragraph names `verification.ts` as the module the FUTURE Discovery route must\n517: import — today imported only by this suite and its shape selftest — and scopes the\n518: accept/refusal sentence to the PRODUCT judgements, naming the fixture's bookkeeping\n519: precondition refusals as the exception.\n520: \n521: **[A8] — ACCEPT, FIXED DIFFERENTLY.** Seat A (low): \"The new mirror makes a provisioned\n522: platform admin unconfirmed by reusing email registration, despite the repository's real\n523: provisioning flow creating that user with `email_confirm: true`.\"\n524: Premise verified in the tree: the predecessor's proof script provisions the admin through\n525: `POST /auth/v1/admin/users` with `email_confirm: true` — the only provisioning recipe this\n526: repository records — so the fixture's admin starting unconfirmed contradicts the repository's\n527: own record, and the header note presents that state as natural rather than as contradicted.\n528: The proposed remedy — a live admin-creation check in step 5 — buys a live measurement for a\n529: state NOTHING reads; disproportionate. Fixed differently: `provisionPlatformAdmin` marks its\n530: auth user confirmed at provisioning and mints no verification link (admin creation sends no\n531: email); the header's \"ONE CONSEQUENCE\" paragraph now says the provisioned admin starts\n532: CONFIRMED, mirroring the recorded recipe, that nothing reads this state, and that it is\n533: live-bound by the first item that reads an admin's verified state. The runtime half stays\n534: honestly unbound: the predecessor's transcript ran with confirmations OFF, so it does not\n535: measure the column under the flip — which is why the mirror is labeled by its recipe, never\n536: called live-bound.\n537: \n538: **[A9] — ACCEPT.** Seat A (low): \"The PR body still says the branch is in the plan phase and\n539: that code comes after plan review, although this commit contains the draft implementation under\n540: code review.\"\n541: True — `pr-body.md`'s own text promised \"This body will be brought up to date as the item\n542: moves\" and was not. Fix: the status paragraph states the current truth (draft built, dual code\n543: review ruled, fixes applied, read-only audit and CI ahead of merge); a mechanical syncs the\n544: GitHub pull-request body from the file, as handed, after the close push.\n545: \n546: **[B3] — ACCEPT.** Seat B (low): \"The rewritten header says 'The other four are section C's',\n547: but AT-001.38 (wrong-password rejection) sits in **section B** of the acceptance file\n548: (`at-req-001.md` line 23, under '## B. Email verification'); only .12/.13/.14 are section C's.\"\n549: Verified against the acceptance file — exactly as claimed. One-clause fix in the b-file\n550: header: the other four belong to the session-and-reset leaf (D2.L2), three of them section\n551: C's, the wrong-password id section B's.\n552: \n553: **Removal check:** no ruling removes work. [A5]'s fixed-differently declines a proposed\n554: ADDITION and carries its verification condition above. Nothing contradicts ratified text and\n555: nothing grows scope; there is no founder question.\n556: \n557: **Post-goal record notes (sitting 3).** [A5]'s verify-first condition HELD: the only change\n558: under `supabase/functions/` is the new `_shared/verification.ts`, and `complete-signup` does\n559: not import it — measured by the executor before any fix. Section 1's deferred rate-limit\n560: question is ANSWERED by measurement: the CLI did not push `email_sent = 2` into the auth\n561: container (the container carried `GOTRUE_RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL_SENT=360000`, recorded in\n562: `stack-up.txt` beside the reading), so the file's cap did not bind the run; check (f) passed\n563: honestly and the D-B relief valve did not fire. The proof script's rate-limit comment was\n564: amended in the open so no stated fact contradicts that measurement. Executor invocations this\n565: sitting: two of the permitted three (the goal, reached on its first attempt; the one-comment\n566: truth amendment).\n\n(End of file - total 566 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# AI4DEV-59 (email verification, unverified-write gate) — PLAN\n\n**Sitting 1 of the item: PLAN. Ruled by the `orchestrator` definition on fable (claude-fable-5,\neffort xhigh).**\n\n**Sitting 2 (DRAFT, same definition and model) ruled on gate 1's four findings and amended this\nplan. The rulings are section 7. The amended text below is what gets built; the pre-amendment\ntext is commit `46b7485`.**\n\n**Sitting 3 (FIX AND GOAL, same definition and model) ruled on gate 2's twelve findings — nine\nfrom seat A, three from seat B, two convergent pairs. The rulings are section 8. That sitting\namended step 2's mirror-binding sentence and step 5's done-list; the pre-amendment text is\ncommit `ac33db1`.**\n\n**Chain, derived from the branch**\n(`nirdrang/ai4dev-59-email-verification-and-the-gate-on-unverified-writing-d2l1`):\nAI4DEV-59 (email verification, unverified-write gate) → AI4DEV-52 (verification, sessions and\nreset container) → AI4DEV-50 (auth dev-tree root) → AI4PM-19 (the authentication requirement).\nNo `attr:` label on any of them; product work with an evidence gate above it.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Downloads\\ai4good\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-aa95110cbeab31aa7\\loop\\items\\AI4DEV-59\\plan.md","text":"# AI4DEV-59 (email verification, unverified-write gate) — PLAN\n\n**Sitting 1 of the item: PLAN. Ruled by the `orchestrator` definition on fable (claude-fable-5,\neffort xhigh).**\n\n**Sitting 2 (DRAFT, same definition and model) ruled on gate 1's four findings and amended this\nplan. The rulings are section 7. The amended text below is what gets built; the pre-amendment\ntext is commit `46b7485`.**\n\n**Sitting 3 (FIX AND GOAL, same definition and model) ruled on gate 2's twelve findings — nine\nfrom seat A, three from seat B, two convergent pairs. The rulings are section 8. That sitting\namended step 2's mirror-binding sentence and step 5's done-list; the pre-amendment text is\ncommit `ac33db1`.**\n\n**Chain, derived from the branch**\n(`nirdrang/ai4dev-59-email-verification-and-the-gate-on-unverified-writing-d2l1`):\nAI4DEV-59 (email verification, unverified-write gate) → AI4DEV-52 (verification, sessions and\nreset container) → AI4DEV-50 (auth dev-tree root) → AI4PM-19 (the authentication requirement).\nNo `attr:` label on any of them; product work with an evidence gate above it.\n\n**Manifest:** `loop/decomp/req-001.md`, deliverable D2 leaf L1, revision `0579425`:\n*\"verification flow (all email-capable account types) + unverified-write gate on Discovery\nmessages · verify: AT-001.09,10 · blocked-by: D1.L1\"*. The D1 container is Done on the board\n(its two leaves merged as pull requests #47 and #48), so the blocker is cleared.\n\n**Acceptance ids this leaf owns:** AT-001.09, AT-001.10.\n**Acceptance text (read-only for this item):** `.taskmaster/docs/acceptance/at-req-001.md`\nlines 20–21. Line 22 matters too: **AT-001.11 is retired** — *\"verification-link\nexpiry/single-use/resend semantics are not stated in REQ-001\"* — so no assertion in this item\nmay claim those semantics.\n\n**Ratified product text behind the gate:** the PRD makes email verification *\"the floor for any\nDiscovery message\"* and says vetting is *\"never the Discovery wall\"* (decision-8,\n`.taskmaster/docs/prd-new.md` line 787; also lines 155 and 159, and\n`.taskmaster/docs/prd-mvp.md` line 157).\n\n**Verify command, pinned:** `bun run at:verify req-001 --tier loop --expect`. The fixture\nadapter is a stand-in capped at the loop tier (its own header, `_fixture.ts` lines 7–10;\n`adapterDerivedCapability()` in `tests/at/harness/capabilities.ts`), CI has no database, and the\nrequirement's integration-tier done contract remains AI4PM-19's gate, not this leaf's.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What I verified in the tree before deciding anything\n\n| claim | verdict | evidence (pointer) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Both ids are declared red, pending on this leaf | true | `tests/at/expected/req-001.json` lines 15–16; stubs at `tests/at/suites/req-001/b-verification-and-sessions.test.ts` lines 13 and 15, each `notLanded(LEAF.D2_L1)` |\n| The config flip is reserved for this leaf | true | `supabase/config.toml` line 243 `enable_confirmations = false`; the b-file header (lines 4–7) says turning it on \"is the verification leaf's own change\" |\n| A local mail catcher is enabled | true | `supabase/config.toml` lines 105–108: `[local_smtp]` enabled, web interface on port 54324 |\n| The local stack limits auth emails to 2 per hour | true (as configured) | `supabase/config.toml` line 216, `[auth.rate_limit] email_sent = 2`; whether it binds with the local test mailer is measured in step 5, not assumed |\n| No Discovery product code exists anywhere | true | grep `discovery` over `supabase/`, `src/`, `tests/` — only docs, a harness rubric for another requirement, and this suite's own stub title; the future route is mapped to a `discovery-message` edge function in `.taskmaster/docs/migration-nextjs-to-tanstack-VERIFIED.md` lines 103–105 |\n| The decision-module pattern is established: shipped judgements, fixture storage | true | `supabase/functions/_shared/accounts.ts` header; `_fixture.ts` header and its imports (lines 45–62) |\n| The suite already models \"the hook a later leaf must call\" | true | `hasPlatformAcknowledgment`'s contract comment, `_contract.ts` lines 244–260 — enforcement it cannot build is named as the hook the later leaf calls |\n| The caller-fact-through-shipped-extractor pattern is ratified | true | `_fixture.ts` lines 208–225 (gate-2 ruling R3 of the GitHub leaf): the fixture renders the canonical GoTrue user shape and derives the fact through the shipped extractor |\n| `_pending.ts` header counts will go stale | true | `tests/at/suites/req-001/_pending.ts` lines 3 and 9 say 30 pending / seven written; after this item it is 28 / nine |\n| CI runs typecheck, harness self-tests, at:check and at:verify (loop, --expect) per suite, plus the ownership and reference guards | true | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` |\n| GoTrue with confirmations on issues no session at signup and refuses sign-in until the address is confirmed | **unverified-runtime-claim** | expected GoTrue b